  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p7), which is after the Eliminations column: interfund transfers of 220,000 (200,000 General to Depreciation hidden in Building and grounds; 20,000 General to Activity hidden in Extracurricular) are already removed from receipts and disbursements, so the total column ties. Remaining transfer out 65,000 to the Nutrition Fund recorded as transfers_out (printed inside total disbursements 6,230,908, so receipts 6,773,498 - disbursements lines 6,165,908). Roll-forward: 5,195,423 + 6,773,498 - 6,165,908 - 65,000 = 5,738,013 (beginning/ending are total fund balances; cash 5,029,241 + county treasurer 708,772 = 5,738,013, p5). Other 27,083 split into rental of facilities 9,198 (General Fund budget schedule) and unexplained 17,885 (General Fund Other 7,885 + Depreciation Fund Other 10,000). Business-type: Nutrition Fund (p8-9), receipts 173,786 operating + interest 105; transfer from General Fund 65,000 in transfers_net; 14,713 + 173,891 - 207,746 + 65,000 = 45,858. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position total column (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p10) is the only General Fund schedule in the trimmed PDF (no Exhibit N program-by-object schedule), so used; its Building and grounds 687,414 split into 487,414 spending and 200,000 hidden transfer; its Transfers 85,000 = 65,000 + 20,000 (Extracurricular 20,000 on the statement). Detail totals include transfers (other financing) where printed inside totals. Activity Fund shown on combining schedule (p13); Nutrition Fund has no budget schedule in trimmed PDF. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}